  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;By reason of size, design and siting of the proposed roof extension, the proposed development would result in loss of daylight, sunlight and overshadowing and a perceived sense of enclosure and overbearing impact to the detriment of neighbouring residential occupiers, contrary to Policy LP2 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-ae20d09a-7fff-e8a5-2255-a9ccc18f7b1f&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;By reason of the insufficient internal headroom of bedroom ‘Bed 6’ and its outlook limited to being skywards only, and the communal space failing to be of a high standard to provide primary functions and encourage social amenity for all occupiers simultaneously, the proposed development would fail to provide high-quality accommodation for future occupiers. The proposed development would, therefore, conflict with Policies LP2 and LP22 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-205eeb40-7fff-5738-8a40-c9da003c64bf&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;By reason of the inadequate provision of cycle parking storage which is safe and accessible for all, the proposed development would fail to meet cycle parking standards as required by Policy T5 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy LP42 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-80f3def6-7fff-162b-6b3b-a574e6af5ce4&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;In the absence of a Unilateral Undertaking or a Section 106 Agreement (S106) to secure appropriate rent levels in accordance with the Local Housing Allowance, the development would fail to secure the proposed HMO at an affordable rent level, contrary to Policy LP22 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-f5191c3b-7fff-9493-32c6-5fcd2b8f38cb&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;In the absence of a Unilateral Undertaking or a Section 106 Agreement securing appropriate mitigation by restricting future occupiers of the development from obtaining parking permits within the CPZ, the proposed development would likely exacerbate existing parking stress and congestion on the surrounding highway network. The development would, therefore, be contrary to Policy LP45 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020) and Policy T6 of the London Plan (2021).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;By reason of the bulk, massing, scale and detailed design, which would fail to take reference from the existing architectural character and appearance of the existing property, the proposed roof extension would appear as an incongruous enlargement to the host property and wider terrace, to the detriment of the character and appearance of the host property and the surrounding area. The proposed development would, therefore, conflict with Policies D1 of the London Plan (2021); Policy LP1 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020); and the guidance as contained within the Council’s Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2025).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
